      "provenance": "Pleiades",
      "associationCertaintyURI": "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/association-certainty/certain",
      "start": 1500,
      "details": "<p><em>Ba\u1e25r-i F\u0101rs</em> (Persian Gulf):\u00a0It is a sea that emerges from the northern side of the <em>Ba\u1e25r-i Hind</em> (Indian Ocean).\u00a0To the east of <em>Mekr\u0101nt\u012bz</em> (Makran coast region), at the source of the <em>Ba\u1e25r-i F\u0101rs</em>, it appears visibly like a mouth (<em>deh\u0101n</em>).\u00a0Likewise, the city of <em>\u2018Umm\u0101n</em> (Oman) is seen on the western side of this sea, and it too is discernible at its mouth, that is, its strait.\u00a0From there it extends, running along the <em>\u2018Umm\u0101n</em> (Oman) coast, and from <em>\u2018Abb\u0101d\u0101n</em> (Abadan, Iran) to <em>Mehr\u016bb\u0101n</em> (Mahru\u0304ba\u0304n, near modern Bushehr).\u00a0Then it passes to <em>S\u012bn\u012bz</em> (modern Bushehr/Old Siniz) and stretches southward until it reaches <em>\u1e2aayy\u0101be</em> (Khabbah / Khaybah).\u00a0From there it proceeds to <em>Seyf\u00fc\u2019l-ba\u1e25r</em> (\u201cthe Sword of the Sea,\u201d Fars coast), and to its east is <em>S\u012br\u0101f</em> (Siraf, Iran).\u00a0From that point, it continues along broken mountain ranges and high desert passes and hills, and then, moving further east, it winds around to <em>\u1e24\u0131\u1e63n Ibn \u2018Amm\u0101re</em> (Hisn Ibn \u2018Amm\u0101ra) and reaches <em>H\u00fcrm\u00fcz</em> (Hormuz), which is the port of <em>Kirm\u0101n</em> (Kerman).\u00a0After that, it stretches toward the southeastern direction, reaching the Makran coast and <em>\u1e32a\u1e63\u1e63at\u012bz</em>.\u00a0[translation]</p>",
